# argus needs no .env.
#
# The one secret the loop uses, SLACK_TOKEN, lives in the credentials file shared with
# Foundry and Pensieve so it is typed once per Mac:
#
#   ~/.config/liamai/env          KEY=value lines, mode 600 (override the path: LIAMAI_ENV)
#
# `./scripts/bootstrap.sh env` creates it and prompts for the token; Foundry's
# `foundry auth --slack` writes the same file. slack-digest's slack-pull.ts reads it
# itself, so nothing is exported into the shell.
#
# A local .env (gitignored; Bun loads it for every `bun …` script) still works and
# overrides the shared file — useful for a one-off token. Slack scopes either way:
# channels:history + users:read (a user token also needs channels:read).
#
# SLACK_TOKEN=xoxp-…
